    "result_text": "All **50 tests pass** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS, zero failures or errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and rewired the household logic accordingly. Four changes across three files:\n\n**1. `OwnerMapper.householdId`** \u2014 now returns the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` (normalized last name = trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased; missing postcode \u2192 empty string). Previously it hashed `lastName + address` with an `HH-` prefix. This feeds `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) as before, so owners with the same last name and postcode now share the household id automatically.\n\n**2. `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 `sharesHousehold` now only *bypasses the duplicate block* rather than creating the link:\n- Added `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate(owner)`, which rejects a create (409 via the existing `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`) when an existing owner has the same computed `householdId`. It's skipped when the request sets `sharesHousehold`, and only applies when a postcode is present.\n- The identity (telephone) collision check still runs unconditionally and is **not** bypassed by `sharesHousehold` (so a repeated telephone still 409s \u2014 Cp28).\n- A declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is no longer flagged as a possible duplicate \u2014 `findPossibleDuplicate` is suppressed for it (Cp35).\n\n**3. `ClinicServiceImpl.countHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 the household-size input now keys on `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`, matching how the household id is computed.\n\nBehavior now matches the spec: two owners sharing last name + postcode are the same household \u2014 the second is rejected as a 409 household duplicate unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member (sharing the household id) and is not flagged as a possible duplicate. Duplicate detection and the household-size count both key off the computed household id.\n\nOne note: the `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` still carries its value in a field named `address` (its debug log prints `address=2000`, which is really the postcode) and the 409 body's `errors` array still lists `[\"lastName\",\"address\"]`. No test asserts on that body, so I left the exception untouched to keep the change tightly scoped \u2014 flag it if you'd like the field/label renamed to `postcode` for accuracy.",
